<h1>ShieldOn — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: June 23, 2026</p>

<p>ShieldOn ("the app") is a parental control app that helps protect children
from inadvertently viewing explicit content on their Android device. This
policy explains what the app does, what permissions it uses, and — most
importantly — what happens to your data.</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p><strong>ShieldOn does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data,
images, or screen content to any server. All analysis happens entirely
on-device. There are no servers. Nothing ever leaves your phone.</strong></p>

<h2>What ShieldOn does</h2>
<p>When activated by a parent or guardian, ShieldOn monitors a configurable
list of apps. While one of those apps is in the foreground, ShieldOn
periodically captures the screen and analyzes it on-device using a local
machine learning model to detect explicit/adult content. If such content is
detected, ShieldOn displays a blur overlay over the screen until the
monitored app is closed.</p>

<h2>Permissions used, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Accessibility Service</strong> — used solely to capture
  on-screen images for on-device analysis, and to detect which app is
  currently in the foreground. ShieldOn does not read, log, or transmit text,
  passwords, or any other accessibility-exposed content. This permission is
  used exclusively for the parental-control screening described above.</li>
  <li><strong>Display over other apps (overlay)</strong> — used to draw the
  blur overlay that covers detected explicit content.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage Access / Foreground app detection</strong> — used to know
  which app is currently active, so monitoring only runs while a selected app
  is in use.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data collection and storage</h2>
<p>ShieldOn does not collect, store, transmit, sell, or share any data of any
kind. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
  <li>No screenshots or captured frames are ever saved to disk, uploaded, or
  retained beyond the instant they are analyzed in memory.</li>
  <li>No analysis results, scores, or logs are sent anywhere outside the
  device.</li>
  <li>ShieldOn has no backend server, no analytics SDK, and no advertising
  SDK.</li>
  <li>All machine learning inference runs locally on the device's own
  hardware (CPU/NPU) using an on-device model. No internet connection is
  required or used for content analysis.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>ShieldOn is designed to be installed and configured by a parent or
guardian on a child's device, for the sole purpose of protecting that child
from explicit content. ShieldOn does not knowingly collect any personal
information from children, because it does not collect personal information
from anyone — see "Data collection and storage" above.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this same
URL with a revised "Last updated" date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
